<<~ ahu #/the-ground>>

! The Growing Rhizome ~ anon floor to two launches

!! The Ground ~ must fall back to anon

Every vessel — a browser at elyncia.app, a node at a Lararium, any device — ''stands anon at its floor'': its own veiled-key, its own local content, no group, and it MUST always return there. Caps, node infrastructure, Handle memberships stack ABOVE the floor; none dissolves it. The whole mesh rests on this one unremovable ground (<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/the-veil-ladder#/the-base-model>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-rhizome>>

!! The Rhizome ~ additive overlays, grown one operator at a time

Each rung rides as an OPTIONAL overlay ON the floor; burning any overlay drops the vessel back to anon, its own content whole. No root grants a rung — every edge signs peer-to-peer (inversion-of-control); relays ''carry'' by treaty, never adjudicate (#the-base-model, the three axes). The rhizome spreads bottom-up:

\ranks rhizome anon-vessel@floor -> known-user@personaGroup -> operator@lararium -> cabal@multi-principal -> nexus@confederation -> DreamNet@super-mesh

* ''anon vessel'' — one device, own key, own content. The floor. Every visitor to either surface starts here.
* ''known-user'' — a PersonaGroup of a human's OWN vessels, sharing doc-syncs (the crossing, `persona-crossing`). Single-principal; converges under one ordering authority.
* ''operator'' — a known-user who RUNS a node vessel + local infrastructure (a Lararium) and relays. The rhizome node; the scale ladder's first rung (<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture>>).
* ''cabal'' — a multi-principal Circle (operators + users share a charter and corpus). Rides CGKA under bounded concurrency (`cabal-two-human`); the tie-break narrows to the add-while-remove window, which accept-and-heal covers for a small cabal.
* ''nexus → DreamNet'' — Lararia federating by treaty; the super-mesh of all nexuses. No global now; each Lararium a causal island.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/two-surfaces>>

!! Two Surfaces ~ one stack, two admission dials

The closed↔open choice runs as ONE NUMBER, never two codebases — the admission-price law prices a crossing as a cost-dial (`admission-price`: high bar reads invite-only, low bar reads open, the same fold spans both). So the two launches run the ''identical'' stack at different bar settings:

* ''amorphousdreams.net → CLOSED beta'' — the ''Amorphous Dreams Cabal'': the first cabal, community-owned from inception, quorum-bootstrapped (the operator + Freyja's personas), ''invite-only'' (`cabal-invite` invite-only policy · the price bar high · a valid vouch required). The seed community; the DreamNet principal. Its content path stands proven (`cabal-two-human`, the two-human crossing).
* ''elyncia.app → OPEN beta'' — the public DreamNet mesh: the same instruments at a ''lower dial'' (the price bar turned toward open). Anon users land, take an anon vessel, read public content, post, and climb the veil-ladder (throwaway → lived → pledged Handle). The broad entry.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-holds-what-owes>>

!! What Holds · What Owes ~ the launch critical path

''Proven + canon-true'' (this session's floor): the base model · the @catalog content crossing (add-before-encrypt, forward-only, burn cuts future-not-history) · the two-human cabal under bounded concurrency · the joinee-side admit wiring (`capEvents` → @daemon → hydrate) · the admission instruments (`cabal-invite` / `admission-price` / `vouch-dag`).

''Owed on the launch critical path'':
* ''make the crossing LIVE'' — the Option-A founder-side wiring (the daemon mints membership via `packPersonaCrossing`; the CLI forwards over the socket; the joinee's keyhive card rides the handshake). Ruled by the web3 elders (BeeKEM requires a live-member adder; ssh-agent shape).
* ''encrypt-on-write'' — the second E2E layer at `resolveOrMintBinding`, so shared content crosses as ciphertext, not membership-gated plaintext.
* ''the admission dial, wired'' — feed `admission-price` from a live vouch ledger so the closed→open number turns per surface.
* ''the browser anon vessel + the relay gate'' — the anon floor at both web surfaces; the V3 proof-of-possession gate STAYS (a channel-bound anti-relay layer, per the elders), the browser↔node crossing awaiting a live key-dump.

The identity-privacy hardening (per-handle vessel credential · scope-exclusive nym · the threshold privacy plane) rides ABOVE the launch floor — owed, but not blocking the closed beta.

<<~/ahu>>

